<title>UK: ACPC begins technical talks in London.</title>
<headline>ACPC begins technical talks in London.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Association of Coffee Producing Countries (ACPC) technical group opened a meeting on Friday to look at export figures and commitments, delegates said.</p>
<p>&quot;We will be looking at export figures for the 1995-96 period and for the early 1996-97 period,&quot; said one ACPC delegate.</p>
<p>The ACPC last met in May when it agreed a new plan to limit green coffee exports from its members to 53.5 million (60 kg) bags in the year to June 1997 against 45.8 million in the previous 12 months.</p>
<p>The ACPC has said that preliminary figures show exports from the group in 1995-96 reached 47 million bags.</p>
<p>The technical group is made up of representatives of El Salvador, Brazil, Ivory Coast, Colombia, Uganda and Indonesia.</p>
<p>The ASPC council will meet on Saturday but delegates said they did not expect any major policy announcements.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7729</p>
